child, so the parent's repos deliverable has a named owner and this leaf's narrowing is auditable.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent child decomposition: 'The ticket repos field — schema, reducer projection, its create-time argument, and the inbound defaulting that fills it from the mapping for tickets arriving from a tracker.'","Leaf Approach: '`repos` stays freely editable on the same edit path — it never reaches the tracker, so there is no binding to invalidate.' — the leaf covers schema/reducer/create+edit args but is silent on inbound defaulting.","Narrowing rationale: inbound defaulting depends on the mapping store (parent root child 'The project mapping store' / multi-project inbound fetch), so deferring it out of this create-time-fields story is plausible — but the leaf does not say so."],"finding":"The parent's 'Ticket repos field' child scopes it to include 'the inbound defaulting that fills it from the mapping for tickets arriving from a tracker', but this leaf — which absorbs the repos field — omits inbound defaulting and does not name a sibling that carries it, leaving that portion of the parent's repos deliverable unassigned in the plan text.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff81be49e5d52cd7a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (repos field); parent child 'The ticket repos field'","norm_id":"nf33be3d46b8806a0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket ingested from a tracker needs its repos populated from the store mapping; if no ticket owns that defaulting, the parent's repos deliverable is incompletely realized."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add one line to the Approach or Scope noting that repos inbound-defaulting from the store mapping is out of scope here and carried by the multi-project inbound fetch child (algebraic-illstarred-mollusk), since it depends on the m